&lt;h2&gt;🚀&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Join fiskaly! Help Us Build Trust in Compliance &amp;amp; Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our squads ship fast, with AI-assisted tooling, on a regulated fiscalization platform that customers trust with their compliance. We want security to keep pace with that speed, not stand in front of it. We are looking for a Senior Security Engineer (Application &amp;amp; Platform Security) to be our founding security engineer in a company of about 150 people. This is a builder's role: you will write the controls that make the secure path the fast path, then prove they work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;💼&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node="10"&gt;As a Senior individual contributor, you will own the secure baseline for cloud, Kubernetes and application delivery, and you will express it as code rather than documents. You will bring threat modelling into squad design reviews, buy and steer external testing, and act as our named security incident commander. You will work closely with Compliance by supplying the technical facts they need, while the regulatory relationship stays with them. You will have read access to all repositories and staging environments, with break-glass production access under audit. You will have no direct reports; you will influence through standards, coaching and well-argued written advice.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;🛠️&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secure Baseline as Code:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and maintain the secure baseline for cloud, Kubernetes and application delivery as policy-as-code and archetype defaults, so squads inherit the control instead of waiting for a review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Threat Modelling:&lt;/strong&gt; Run threat modelling inside squad design reviews for changes that touch data flows, authentication, authorisation or cryptography.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Assurance:&lt;/strong&gt; Own assurance end to end: scope external tests, triage findings, drive remediation to a verified fix and run the retest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Command:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as named security incident commander. Maintain the severity model and runbook, coordinate response, preserve evidence and supply the facts for Compliance's notification decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-Assisted Testing:&lt;/strong&gt; Operate our AI-assisted security testing programme: run it, score it, tune it, and decide when it is not worth the triage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champions &amp;amp; Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Re-charter and run the security champions guild, and turn recurring squad friction into platform improvements together with Foundational Infrastructure, Observability, Compliance and Delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor &amp;amp; Data Review:&lt;/strong&gt; Review external vendor changes that would put customer data in a new place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure &amp;amp; Publish:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the security metrics, including publishing the function's own misses, and measure the friction security adds to delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;✨&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls Shipped as Code:&lt;/strong&gt; You have shipped security controls as code (policy, CI checks, IaC guardrails), not only advised on them. You have hands-on experience with Kyverno or OPA and with GitHub Actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Security Depth:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong grounding in threat modelling, authentication, authorisation, cryptography misuse and injection classes, plus data classification and redaction design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud &amp;amp; Kubernetes Fluency:&lt;/strong&gt; You read Terraform/OpenTofu, Kubernetes manifests and Helm without assistance, and you know cloud IAM and Kubernetes security boundaries well enough to write a baseline engineers can actually implement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pentest Ownership as the Client:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience scoping and running penetration tests from the buying side: writing the scope, judging the report and driving remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First-Security-Hire Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; You have been the first or only security person somewhere, ideally in a regulated or otherwise high-trust environment, and you can describe what you deliberately did not do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Enough familiarity with the German regulatory landscape to sit in a BSI / KassenSichV conversation without owning the programme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; You use AI tooling for drafting, triage and policy generation with review discipline, and you can say where it fails. You understand AI-specific attack surface: prompt injection against agents that read code, agent credential scope and model supply chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Writing &amp;amp; Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; You write more than you talk, and prefer a one-page decision note to a 20-slide deck. You bring a proposed control with an adoption plan and a cost, never a mandate. You are comfortable saying "that is advice, not a veto", and you build relationships with squad engineers before asking them to change anything.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
