&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact is a data and AI services company with around 2,500 people across 36 offices. We are part of Anthropic's Claude Partner Network and have rolled out Claude across our own organization, so our advice to clients comes from running it ourselves first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DeployCo is Artefact's team dedicated to deploying Claude at scale inside enterprises. It works through three levers. Deployment and adoption gets organizations from a few early adopters to company-wide use. Process reimagination redesigns core workflows around agentic AI. Agent production ships working agents into client systems. Forward Deployed Engineers are the builders behind the third lever and the technical backbone of the other two.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an FDE you join a client's own AI or engineering team as a builder, not an advisor. You design, code, and ship production-grade Claude solutions directly inside their stack, following their conventions, repositories, and CI. You also leave the capability behind, so that when the engagement ends the client's engineers can extend and maintain what was built without us.&lt;br&gt;The work ranges from short, intense engagements, like standing up a governed Claude Code deployment in a few weeks, to longer embeds where you become the technical anchor of a multi-agent portfolio and a larger Artefact pod grows around you. This is a senior role, and we expect you to own technical direction on an engagement from the first week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you'll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build production agents. Design and deploy Claude-based agents and workflows that run in production, with the engineering standards that implies. That means tests, error handling, monitoring, and cost control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect Claude to enterprise systems. Build custom MCP servers and connectors to business applications and data sources, enforcing the client's own access rules. This includes permissions, traceability, and segregation of rights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer the context layer. Contribute to Artefact's context platform approach, including deterministic authentication before data reaches the model, user-level context injection, and observability for token spend and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy and govern Claude Code. Set up SSO and role-based access, managed settings, approved MCP servers and plugin marketplaces, permission modes, sandboxing, and OpenTelemetry-based usage monitoring. Help clients choose between deployment options (Team, Enterprise, cloud providers, gateways) based on security, data residency, and cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable skills. Turn client workflows into Claude Skills and shared skills libraries that teams can find, reuse, and build on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable client engineers. Pair program, review code, document patterns, and deliver hands-on Claude Code training and labs, sometimes to cohorts of dozens of developers and sometimes to CTOs and engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed the product loop. Capture deployment pitfalls and product feedback from the field and share it with Anthropic through our partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior-level experience in software engineering or data science, with production systems you have shipped and operated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recent, hands-on work with the GenAI stack, going beyond prototypes. This includes tool use, agent design, retrieval, evaluation, and prompt and context engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated depth with Claude in particular, such as Claude Code, the Claude API, Skills, or MCP, and a point of view on how the stack is evolving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python or TypeScript, and solid grounding in enterprise integration, including APIs, identity and access management (SSO, OAuth, SCIM), and cloud platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in client-facing settings, explaining technical trade-offs to engineers and to non-technical stakeholders, and running a workshop when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in German and English&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anthropic certification (Claude Certified Developer or Architect) is welcome but not expected, since it is usually only available through a partner company. We support you in earning it once you join.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and securing MCP servers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in security, observability (OpenTelemetry), or FinOps for AI workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated industries such as banking, asset management, or pharma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of teaching or technical training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct work with Anthropic's partner and applied AI teams, including co-delivered labs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Varied, high-impact engagements across EMEA in finance, retail, industry, and consumer goods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear path from FDE to technical anchor of a full AI delivery pod&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification support and dedicated learning time&lt;/li&gt;
